.chapter 7
.h1 Large documents [large]
The project made large documents with scripts and ran the Editor and the
Printer on them.  No limit was reached at 4,062 pages.
.h2 Documents [large-record]
The large documents are four.  The Twain collection is the complete works of
Mark Twain from Project Gutenberg, 15.6 MB.  The synthetic manuals big4062 (150
chapters, 4,062 PDF pages, 13,041,779 bytes) and big1219 (45 chapters, 1,219
pages, 3,899,341 bytes) are made.  The Reference Manual (753 pages, 2,212,980
bytes, 17,945 items, 1,295 headlines, 135 pictures) is the manual of Strata as
one document.
The Twain collection has @pages_whole@ pages at @words_per_page@ words each, and
the Printer makes @pdf_pages_whole@; the commit of 12 November counts 4,620
without saying how.  The project recorded no hand test of this document.  Its
record is the runs of the measuring script and the work that they caused
({x:memory-first}).
.h2 Method [large-tested]
One script makes the synthetic manuals from chapter sources with a fixed seed.
Another makes the documents of the memory measurement from a text, as plain
documents and as structured documents with a section for every 25 pages.
A program runs the commands of the Editor on a large document without a
terminal and times each command and the layout that the next screen needs.  A
script runs the Editor in a pseudo-terminal and times every key until the
screen is quiet.  The Printer runs on the whole document, on a range of
sections and by the DVI route.  The check reads each PDF: every row of the
contents and of the index gives the page of its headline (1,165 and 4,713 rows
for the Reference Manual), no cross reference is left as question marks and no
page is blank.
.h2 Results [large-numbers]
{Tab:bigdocs} gives the Editor and the Printer on three documents.  The machine
has eight threads and 15 GB of memory, and times are wall clock.  The
measurement is older than the memory work of {x:memory}.
.tabcap bigdocs The Editor and the Printer on three large documents
.table 33 7 8 12
Measure | manual | big1219 | big4062
Pages of the PDF | 753 | 1,219 | 4,062
Load the document (ms) | 33 | 45 | 151
First layout (ms) | 78 | 92 | 303
Memory after the layout, peak (MB) | 28 | 38 | 123
Search from the start to the end (ms) | 80 | 97 | 330
Type a character, with the layout (ms) | 6.6 | 9.5 | 36
Save (ms) | 66 | 81 | 444
The whole PDF (s) | 44.4 | 29.7 | 98.9
LaTeX passes | 2 | 2 | 2
The largest process, pdfTeX (MB) | 36 | 36 | 114
.end
The DVI file of the Reference Manual, 753 pages and 5.9 MB, opens in the Viewer
in 0.32 s; the slowest page takes 55 ms to draw.
.h2 Limits [large-limits]
The record lists what could have had a fixed size, and none was reached: counts
of items, blocks, headlines, cross references and index entries; 16-bit values
of the layout, which use 32 bits when a distance does not fit; page numbers up
to 99,999.  TeX printed 4,062 pages in 114 MB without "capacity exceeded".  The
changes were for time: the quadratic search of cross references
({x:memory-first}).
